      text: 'The protocol should be prepared in light of the circumstances concerning the spouses’ children, if any, and their property. Not every case requires the same provisions; however, clearly stating the matters the parties have agreed on can help reduce later disagreements over interpretation.\n\n\n\nIf the parties have children together, the protocol should address custody, contact arrangements, and child support. It should also address spousal support and compensation where relevant. If the parties have reached an agreement, they may also include provisions on property, jewelry, household items, joint debts, and litigation expenses.',
