      text: 'Property division may be addressed in an uncontested divorce protocol. If the parties have reached an agreement, the assets covered—such as real estate, vehicles, bank accounts, company shares, household items, or jewelry—and how they will be divided should be described as specifically as possible.\n\n\n\nA general statement such as “the parties have divided their property” may not clearly identify which assets or claims are covered. If the parties have agreed to transfer real estate, make a payment, or deliver an item, it is helpful to identify the relevant asset and explain when and how the transaction will take place. Details concerning title, transfer, delivery, or cost allocation may also be included in accordance with the parties’ agreement.\n\n\n\nFor jewelry and personal belongings, the protocol should state who will keep each item, whether any items will be returned, and whether either party has any further claim concerning them.',
