      title: "Which acts may be challenged in an annulment action?",
      text: "An annulment action may be brought against a final and enforceable unilateral administrative act that produces legal consequences for individuals. Whether an act is reviewable depends on factors such as its finality, enforceability, and whether the claimant’s legally protected interest is affected.",
