  introText: "The essential purpose of the mediation process is to reduce the solution agreed by the parties to a written document. The settlement agreement drawn up at the end of the process is binding on the parties and may give rise to certain consequences if it is not performed. It is therefore important that the content of the document be prepared carefully, that the obligations be set out clearly, and that the enforceability regime be understood.",
