  introText: "An individual application to the Constitutional Court is an extraordinary remedy available to persons alleging that an act, action, or omission of public authority has violated a right protected under the common scope of the Constitution and the European Convention on Human Rights. It is not a general appeal or a request for a retrial. For an application to be examined, the admissibility requirements set by law must be met and the alleged violation must be explained specifically.",
